---
description: Implement all stakeholder-approved Pincushion pins — one at a time, claim → code → resolve → commit
alwaysApply: false
---

1. Call `implement_approved_pins` to fetch every approved pin grouped by page, with element selectors, suggested branch names, and full thread context.
2. For each pin:
   - `claim_pin` to mark it implementing (so other agents don't double-claim)
   - Use the element selector + textContent to locate the source code
   - Read the thread to understand what the stakeholder wants
   - Make the code change
   - `fix_and_resolve` to close it with a one-line summary of what changed (no thread comment — the commit is the record)
3. Commit per pin, not in batches. Suggested branch comes back in the response.

If there are no approved pins, say so and offer to run `/pins` to see what's still in `ready` waiting for approval.
